AC2 — backend APIGuestMiddleware X-Guest-Token header read (falsifiable differential)
Guest id=345 (holds a real token). Same shared DB; only the middleware code differs by port.
Headers: zoneId:[1] moduleId:1 X-localization:en lat/long set.

PRE-CHANGE backend :8000 (primary tree, NO X-Guest-Token read):
  CASE 1 header-only (X-Guest-Token, no query token)   -> HTTP 401   (old code ignores the header)
  CASE 2 legacy guest_token in query (no header)       -> HTTP 200   (old query path)

POST-CHANGE backend :8001 (worktree, reads X-Guest-Token first):
  CASE 1 header-only (X-Guest-Token, no query token)   -> HTTP 200   (header authenticates)
  CASE 2 legacy guest_token in query (no header)       -> HTTP 200   (fallback retained, non-breaking)
  CASE 3 WRONG X-Guest-Token value                     -> HTTP 401   (header is genuinely evaluated, not presence-only)
  CASE 4 no token at all (guest_id only)               -> HTTP 401   (strict guard for a token-holding guest)

Conclusion: the change is exactly what enables header auth; legacy query fallback preserved; wrong-token still rejected.

LIVE app capture (UserApp on emulator-5556 -> logging proxy -> :8001), guest id=346:
  POST /api/v1/customer/cart/add?guest_id=346
    X-Guest-Token = PRESENT (GVWzjEij..)      Authorization = ABSENT
    guest_token_in_query = False              guest_token_in_body = False
    body = {"item_id":6,"price":"4.5","quantity":1,...}   (no guest_token field)
    RESP 200 (5161 bytes)  -> backend authenticated the guest from the header, live from the app
  GET /api/v1/customer/cart/list?guest_id=346  X-Guest-Token=PRESENT  guest_token_in_query=False  -> 200
